{"type": "mcq", "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A rectangle has an area of <math alttext=\"3,168\"><mn>3,168</mn>\n</math> square inches. What is the area, in <strong>square feet</strong>, of this rectangle? <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 1 foot  equals 12 inches right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>foot</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mtext>&#160;inches</mtext></mrow></mfenced></math></p>", "keys": ["f3b48414-2edb-46da-a295-b3db3c9207e4"], "answerOptions": [{"id": "f3b48414-2edb-46da-a295-b3db3c9207e4", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"22\"><mn>22</mn>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "17cb1968-fa0f-487d-8692-9a729868d913", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"56.3\"><mn>56.3</mn>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "9c18c769-b875-415e-9ea7-8a2688c3ddbd", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"264\"><mn>264</mn>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "78096205-7c99-4a01-9919-fd5d16d25330", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"675.4\"><mn>675.4</mn>\n</math></p>"}], "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"1 foot  equals 12 inches\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>foot</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>inches</mtext></math>. It follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"1 squared square foot  equals 12 squared square inches\"><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>square&#160;foot</mtext><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>12</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>square&#160;inches</mtext></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"1 square foot  equals 144 square inches\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>square&#160;foot</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>144</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>square&#160;inches</mtext></math>. Thus,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3,168\"><mn>3,168</mn></math> square inches is equivalent to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 3,168 square inches right parenthesis left parenthesis StartFraction 1 square foot Over 144 square inches EndFraction right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>3,168</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>square&#160;inches</mtext><mo>)</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>square&#160;foot</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>144</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>square&#160;inches</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"22\"><mn>22</mn></math> square feet.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect. This is the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 3,168 Over 12 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>3,168</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></math>, not <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 3,168 Over 144 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>3,168</mn><mn>144</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>", "externalid": "16d02cf9-fae4-4096-a277-a897cfed31be", "correct_answer": ["A"]}